{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater","id":131497,"title":"How do you kill a Sin-Eater?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-10T21:01:04-07:00","id":131497,"title":"How do you kill a Sin-Eater?","content":"The topic says it all. What are ways to keep a sin-eater permanently dead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T23:48:44-07:00","id":131741,"title":"","content":"Kill him enough times or sever his connection to his Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T02:00:34-07:00","id":131923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=131741#post131741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kill him enough times or sever his connection to his Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really with the first as you would tend to get the split personality thing going.<br /> <br /> I think this is the main thing that was centrally missing on Mortal Remains.<br /> <br /> I'm tempted to combine the Effigy tactic with Giest. When the Sin-Eater goes down, The Giest can be summoned via the Effigy tactic and be proceeded to be beaten the shit out of, and either dumped into the Underworld or put into cursed items/relics the same way Werewolves treat spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 05-11-2014, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T02:48:53-07:00","id":131992,"title":"","content":"Find a Dead Domain with a Law that prevents Sin-Eaters from leaving, toss them in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T03:06:14-07:00","id":131994,"title":"","content":"Flush their ashes down the toilet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T03:09:30-07:00","id":131996,"title":"","content":"Damage the host badly enough that the Geist abandons the flesh to its fate. A comatose Sin-eater can't be regenerated, and if memory serves, is as restricted as any other mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T05:56:21-07:00","id":132076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=131923#post131923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really with the first as you would tend to get the split personality thing going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being that my rereading treadmill literally got to the third chapter of Geist Core <i>yesterday</i>\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geist: the Sin-Eaters Core Rulebook, page 173, sidebar, &quot;The Wretched&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The soul of a Sin-Eater is stretched and torn by the abrupt return to life forced upon him by his geist. With too many deaths and returns, the soul can be reduced to tatters. Sin-Eaters that have their maximum potential Synergy reduced to zero become nothing more than human-shaped meat-suits for the geist inside them. <b>At this point most geists reluctantly allow the body to die, rather than share it with the sobbing remnants of the Sin-Eater\u2019s soul. Some geists hold on for too long, though, and eventually the shattered soul drives it insane. The Sin-Eaters call these unfortunates the Wretched.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The Wretched are a risk, not an inevitability\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geist: the Sin-Eaters Core Rulebook, page 177, The Art of Necromancy - Eaters of the Dead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This particular form of cannibalism is taboo within Sin-Eater culture: Not only does it place geists at risk, but <b>the only real way to devour a geist that has bonded to a host is to slay the host.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026and the geist being most separate from its Bound while the latter is dead is in line with the fiction:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Book of the Dead, page 6, Ascent</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pain exploded in her head. The pain in her head subsided, and with it all memory\u2026 no! She forced herself to remember.<br /> <b>\u200b\u201cYou shot me,\u201d she whispered.<br /> \u200b\u200bReese turned his head and in the florescent light of the dig she saw he was wearing a deathmask. A patrician nose jutted out of the deathmask, grotesquely overstated, over a bushy mustache made of bristling steel wool. Long streaks of crimson ran down from the eyeholes and over the paunchy cheeks.<br /> \u200b\u201cMr. White.\u201d [Her geist.]</b><br /> \u200b\u201cHe kept you from me,\u201d Reese said. The Harridan cackled under his words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the timer on Sin-Eater resurrection remains &quot;next dawn/dusk,&quot; so any means of permanently killing a Sin-Eater is going to by necessity involve, y'know, killing the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T06:18:24-07:00","id":132088,"title":"","content":"My vote comes down to slaying the Sin-Eater, then performing an exorcism over the remains to banish the Geist back to the Underworld. This is roughly similar to how the ritual for one of the ex-Sin-Eaters to steal a Geist works. <br /> <br /> The main reason that exorcisms don't work on Sin-Eaters is because, well, removing a major template is a bad thing. But slaying one of the Bound and keeping it dead? No reason that shouldn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T07:43:26-07:00","id":132249,"title":"","content":"The limit to the number of times they can resurrect is five with wretched being a possibility but it's GM fiat, and the resurrection bit isn't really all that it's cracked up to be without the rest of their powers. It's figuring out how to deal with their other powers that should be the priority, then you can just shoot 'em until they stay dead, <i>or they pretend their permanently dead</i>.<br /> <br /> +1 for MCN's idea though, I also recommend Mortal Remains rules which makes willpower their power source instead of plasm cause that way willpower affecting abilities cripple them. Plus more limited bulwarking if that's a deal breaker for you.<br /> <br /> *EDIT*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 05-11-2014, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T12:49:21-07:00","id":134238,"title":"","content":"Chain them up and starve them out. If the Geist wants to revive them, well, they're still chained up. Eventually it'll give up.<br /> Although you probably shouldn't be around when they come back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:31:12-07:00","id":135825,"title":"","content":"The same way you teach krogans of compassion. You will need many bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T04:40:59-07:00","id":145518,"title":"","content":"Or you know, do something to them that it doesn't matter whether they're resurrected or not. Bury them in concrete and build a building on top of them, lock them in a trunk and compact the car, stuff like that. Just because the geist can resurrect the sin-eater doesn't mean it can get the sin-eater out of the situation that killed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T16:43:26-07:00","id":149022,"title":"","content":"The problem with that sort of strategy (and several others presented here) is that when a Geist resurrects a sin-eater, they aren't limited to restoring life to the original body. (Unlike what happens during the Bargain.) If you chop up their corpse and spread it across the woods, they'll just show up at the next dawn or dusk with a functional body, albeit one that's mostly full of agg damage.<br /> <br /> Similarly, you can't keep a sin-eater in a comatose state, because the only times they actually lose consciousness is when they're asleep or dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T03:53:22-07:00","id":149299,"title":"","content":"I don't remember that tidbit, is that part of the updated geist book are am I just having a senior moment at the ripe old age of 37?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T05:29:22-07:00","id":149325,"title":"","content":"Sin Eaters are so in tune with death that until they die they cannot lose consciousness outside of sleep. It's on pages 172 onward in the &quot;Symbiosis&quot; sub-chapter of the Geist Corebook. Cliff notes:<br /> <br /> - They also can spend Plasm to absorb a certain amount of damage and turn it into Bashing at the end of the scene<br /> - Taking the same damage from a gunshot to the head or disembowelment<br /> - They can also pillage Mementos for health, destroying them in the process<br /> <br /> Killing them for good is hard and if they have Mementos I feel sorry for those that try. And I'm not even going to touch Synergy drops...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T07:02:17-07:00","id":194608,"title":"","content":"Do you guys allow SE to come back after having, like, their head chopped off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3471-silenceremains","name":"silenceremains","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T08:13:37-07:00","id":194636,"title":"","content":"I, personally, let sin-eaters come back even after they've been thrown into industrial furnaces and reduced to ash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T08:30:59-07:00","id":194640,"title":"","content":"How to kill a Sin-Eater: tie him to a chair and shoot him in the head. When he comes back to life, shoot him again. Repeat the process until he doesn\u2019t come back to life.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s the general principle, at least. There are two main flaws with this or similar ideas:<br /> <br /> 1. as was pointed out, shooting a Sin-Eater in the head is no more likely to kill him than shooting him in the arm. <br /> 2. When he comes back to life, someone else dies \u2014 possibly <i>you</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-11-2014, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T08:57:10-07:00","id":194654,"title":"","content":"Same as That Other Guy. Though I will make them wake up in the Underworld if they're truely obliterated (Like reduced to ash and such). Probably crawl out of a river or lake, scream their lungs out. I also let them come back, no matter how many times they're killed, only having them go compleately insane from it. For this reason, Sin-Eaters in my games usually try to solve problems in non-violent ways, even those Sin-Eaters who would normally prefer violence to non-violence. If a Sin-Eater has to be stopped somehow, for whatever reason, they usually go about it by trapping them somehow. There is a Sin-Eater group who work pretty much like Sin-Eater Assassins, and use the Ceremony that detatches Geists from their Sin-Eaters in order to easier kill the Sin-Eater/Geist whoever their target is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T16:40:45-07:00","id":272571,"title":"","content":"Be a Promethean, chop them up, make them a promethean, watch the fireworks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3707-thediabadass","name":"TheDiabadass","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T09:23:33-07:00","id":272968,"title":"","content":"Guaranteed way to get the Geist to give up after a single death of their Sin-Eater is to do something to the Sin-Eater that there is no point bringing them back... The 'buried in concrete' method as mentioned before will soon have the Geist desert their Sin-Eater and be on the look-out for someone else. There are of course Ceremonies for Sin-Eaters to rid Geist from others and do all kinds of nasties to stop one of their own in their tracks... Though thats generally a Synergy 1 sin and a Sacrosanct has likely been taken down more than once beforehand... I don't think any Sin-Eater would go so far as to be on the fast-track to being a Vacant for something so simple if they did at all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:28:06-07:00","id":445717,"title":"","content":"find a meanest, biggest spirit with Ghost Eater numina. Tell him where Geist lives. <br /> Use Soul Jar spell. Offer him as a payment for abyssal investment. <br /> Can tremere eat Geists? or just eat their hosts.<br /> Use a permanent fetish creation on one.<br /> Lure one inside a shadow in a Wound, see what happens.<br /> Find a vampire addicted to ghost essence, let him drain a Geist, see what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T14:44:30-07:00","id":446550,"title":"","content":"Those methods on the whole will likely turn a Bound into one of the Vacant first though, rather than outright kill them. Of course, once the Geist has been expulled from their host, they have nothing to pull them back from death once they've been killed. Do Vacant still have a reserve of plasm though? Because that'll still make it rather tougher than normal to kill a Bound, as they could use what plasm they have left to regenerate wounds, if the plasm isn't something the Geist within held onto, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T23:06:51-07:00","id":447186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=446550#post446550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those methods on the whole will likely turn a Bound into one of the Vacant first though, rather than outright kill them. Of course, once the Geist has been expulled from their host, they have nothing to pull them back from death once they've been killed. Do Vacant still have a reserve of plasm though? Because that'll still make it rather tougher than normal to kill a Bound, as they could use what plasm they have left to regenerate wounds, if the plasm isn't something the Geist within held onto, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think they will have enough awareness left in the first few hours to resist, just repeat whatever you did. Or simply use s magic to bound them as your eternal minions (again, half mad from a horrible experience).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:22:38-07:00","id":447662,"title":"","content":"Three of those would fail automatically because it's directly affecting a major template, the Human and Geist are merged both body and soul into one so singling out the Geist directly while merged is not an option. Unless your talking about a Geist outside on it's own then that defeats the point since it's not a Sin-Eater, the rest works as if your using it on a standard Supernatural soul/being.<br /> <br /> Otherwise yeah that'd probably do it, destroy the soul they won't come back but none of those methods are explicitly noted as bypassing Bulwarking, the only one so far is Etheric Rounds. Although killing them five times is also doable.<br /> <br /> Personally the best way to deal with Sin-Eaters for me was to not even bother killing them and instead imprison them in a helpless situation where they might as well be dead, forever if neccesary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 03-18-2015, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T09:12:02-07:00","id":447761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoeMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=447662#post447662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three of those would fail automatically because it's directly affecting a major template, the Human and Geist are merged both body and soul into one so singling out the Geist directly while merged is not an option. Unless your talking about a Geist outside on it's own then that defeats the point since it's not a Sin-Eater, the rest works as if your using it on a standard Supernatural soul/being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they are merged in body, only soul. I don't see much difference with how spirit claimed operate.Besides I suggested ways to get rid of Geist that I could come up in the moment., human body and damaged soul are easy to deal with. Ultimately it depends on individual ST, the other way would be to get a real Sin-Eater and experiment on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:21:28-07:00","id":447903,"title":"","content":"Yeah it can be hard to tell the difference between different types of soul fusion that isn't semantic wordplay however the most important distinctions in this case is first that Claiming is subsuming the soul through brute force and is basically just possession while the Bargain is a genuine consensual merge between the Geist and soul. Second the host is in control while the Geist can only influence by pestering them. Finally, I say merged body because the Geist is inside the body in a very literal sense (P. 172 Symbiology intro).<br /> <br /> Distinctions aside P. 19 under Merging, Not Possession, explicitly states a Geist can not be exorcised, abjured, or otherwise driven out of the mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:33:48-07:00","id":447935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=194654#post194654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Sin-Eater group who work pretty much like Sin-Eater Assassins, and use the Ceremony that detaches Geists from their Sin-Eaters in order to easier kill the Sin-Eater/Geist whoever their target is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've considered making that a Tactic for Hunters to detach Geists and put it in a soul jar.<br /> <br /> I've been debating if Geists should suffer a drop of one point of essence each day while in the jar until the Geist runs out of the stuff and it starts to drain from the Corpus, in which if the Giest is not let out in time, dies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T13:53:26-07:00","id":448214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoeMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=447903#post447903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it can be hard to tell the difference between different types of soul fusion that isn't semantic wordplay however the most important distinctions in this case is first that Claiming is subsuming the soul through brute force and is basically just possession while the Bargain is a genuine consensual merge between the Geist and soul. Second the host is in control while the Geist can only influence by pestering them. Finally, I say merged body because the Geist is inside the body in a very literal sense (P. 172 Symbiology intro).<br /> <br /> Distinctions aside P. 19 under Merging, Not Possession, explicitly states a Geist can not be exorcised, abjured, or otherwise driven out of the mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Claiming is definitely not possession and it needs not be forceful there are plenty of examples in Book of Spirits. <br /> I am a bit new with Geist. So does any physical manifestations of Geist appear inside the body? Because as far as I could see the flesh wasn't changed. Claimed for example can grow extra hands, scales, staff like that. So Geist stays inside the body and is immune to any other major splat powers to get it out of there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T15:58:06-07:00","id":448395,"title":"","content":"Standard Claiming is generally possession in the sense that the Spirit is the one in control while the human mind (what is left) that isn't merged into the Spirit's is submerged. It also refers to some other similar soul fusion hijinks too, so it gets confusing.<br /> <br /> The Geist's deathly essence permeates the body's flesh which is the Plasm that is in their blood, otherwise the other changes generally can only be perceived through supernatural senses that is attuned to Death, Ghosts, etc. The changes you describe generally only come about through use of Manifestations and Keys. There does exist a twilight illusion of sorts of the Geist that can be perceived but all that means is that you can communicate with it directly but that's about it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The human side can reverse possess the Geist's mind turning them from the physical world into Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 03-18-2015, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T16:01:50-07:00","id":448399,"title":"","content":"Would the soul shredding ritual in mage work? I forget what the spell was called but it basically reached into a person's soul and obliterated it, leaving a hollowed out body that is essentially a vegetable. I mean it would in no way be easy, but wouldn't that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T16:15:33-07:00","id":448438,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's just that for stuff like soul destroying attacks it has to be the killing blow and be un-Bulwarked either by wearing the Sin-Eater down by fully filling up it's health track once with plasm or preventing the Bulwarking. If he dies without those prerequisites his soul is intact. Although it's not quite clear what happens when they die there is the very real possibility the Geist itself will hover around the body until the next resurrection absolutely pissed, and you need as per Book of the Dead both Death and Spirit to affect it.<br /> <br /> But if you ask me that last bit I would recommend being either/or as per ST fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 03-18-2015, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T16:28:56-07:00","id":448451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoeMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=448438#post448438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's just that for stuff like soul destroying attacks it has to be the killing blow and be un-Bulwarked either by wearing the Sin-Eater down by fully filling up it's health track once with plasm or preventing the Bulwarking. If he dies without those prerequisites his soul is intact. Although it's not quite clear what happens when they die there is the very real possibility the Geist itself will hover around the body until the next resurrection absolutely pissed, and you need as per Book of the Dead both Death and Spirit to affect it.<br /> <br /> But if you ask me that last bit I would recommend being either/or as per ST fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the deaht of the Sin-Eater like being cast unconciously into an ocean and the Geist is the lifeguard. With it, you'de drown in this sea of death. However, the Geist can pull you back up to the surface of life, to break for air. However, while he does so, he isn't occupying the coast of life anymore, his down there in the murky depths with you, trying to keep you from drowing.<br /> So in other words, to a Mage, the Sin-Eater dies as usual and the body is truely and entirely dead. Untill the Geist claws the Sin-Eater's soul back to the world of the quick and reverses the final moments of death, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T23:27:18-07:00","id":448885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=448451#post448451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine the deaht of the Sin-Eater like being cast unconciously into an ocean and the Geist is the lifeguard. With it, you'de drown in this sea of death. However, the Geist can pull you back up to the surface of life, to break for air. However, while he does so, he isn't occupying the coast of life anymore, his down there in the murky depths with you, trying to keep you from drowing.<br /> So in other words, to a Mage, the Sin-Eater dies as usual and the body is truely and entirely dead. Untill the Geist claws the Sin-Eater's soul back to the world of the quick and reverses the final moments of death, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> and what happens if you use it as a link to summon them before resurrection? Or use some ritual that prevents them from returning? I think it's some GotV spell to make sure the dead don't talk again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T00:43:52-07:00","id":448908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=448885#post448885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> and what happens if you use it as a link to summon them before resurrection? Or use some ritual that prevents them from returning? I think it's some GotV spell to make sure the dead don't talk again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you summon the Sin-Eaters &quot;ghost&quot; before he is resurrected, I think you'de summon the Geist and Sin-Eater, as a &quot;ghost&quot;. Probably, it would look like an amalgamation between the Sin-Eaters physical form and the Geists Corpus.<br /> Could be a fun spin, that now that its been summoned artificially, so to speak, it cant bring the Sin-Eaters body to life anymore. Of course, now it exists as a Geist/Sin-Eater Ghost-Combi, so theres that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T17:43:10-07:00","id":449940,"title":"","content":"Then again it'd probably just delay the resurrection until whatever is preventing it is undone or summoning it could even actually bypass whatever causes the Synergy Loss if you want be a dick (assuming the Sin-Eater is an antagonist), it depends on how you interpret the stuff about resurrection and how it works for any specifics. One definite thing however is that the resurrection process is damaging to the Human side of the soul and more and more of it is replaced with the Geist each time, the one exception to this is through the four element Oracle Manifestations you die the right way you come back fully healed with no Synergy loss.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the one merit for founders involving unlimited resurrection doesn't indicate that normal Sin-Eaters need a body, the founder needs a body with that merit. Although with Supernal magic you'd only really need the blood and possibly the Keystone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T02:05:36-07:00","id":494522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoeMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=449940#post449940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again it'd probably just delay the resurrection until whatever is preventing it is undone or summoning it could even actually bypass whatever causes the Synergy Loss if you want be a dick (assuming the Sin-Eater is an antagonist), it depends on how you interpret the stuff about resurrection and how it works for any specifics. One definite thing however is that the resurrection process is damaging to the Human side of the soul and more and more of it is replaced with the Geist each time, the one exception to this is through the four element Oracle Manifestations you die the right way you come back fully healed with no Synergy loss.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the one merit for founders involving unlimited resurrection doesn't indicate that normal Sin-Eaters need a body, the founder needs a body with that merit. Although with Supernal magic you'd only really need the blood and possibly the Keystone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> see post #22","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T23:58:13-07:00","id":509659,"title":"","content":"As the guy that first proposed (and later wrote) the idea of making Sin-Eaters nigh impossible to kill for good, this thread is highly entertaining. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My thought was that actually managing to kill a SE should be a big deal, and should come out of the story. I also wanted to give STs a chance to play a bit harder with their PCs than normal, and to more fully explore the death/resurrection theme.<br /> <br /> Personally, I favor ideas that trap SEs in lose-lose situations that would make the Geist want to bugger off, rather than catch-all methods of simply killing the SE. Killing someone is boring, trapping them for all eternity (maybe) seems much more interesting to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>John Newman<br /> Onyx Path Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5213-jn7","name":"JN7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T11:32:41-08:00","id":1014858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JN7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=509659#post509659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing someone is boring, trapping them for all eternity (maybe) seems much more interesting to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or as Bobby Singer said: &quot;That's a problem for Hunters in Space Suits&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:05:30-08:00","id":1040229,"title":"","content":"I just started reading the book, but the text on the top of page 19 says the geist can't heal their sin-eater, it only prevents him from dying. Therefore the body has time to recover, but they can't recover from something that a human body couldn't heal on it's own! <br /> So if the sin-eater is shot in the head, he can't recover his brain, since the body can't do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:13:04-08:00","id":1040240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=1040229#post1040229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just started reading the book, but the text on the top of page 19 says the geist can't heal their sin-eater, it only prevents him from dying. Therefore the body has time to recover, but they can't recover from something that a human body couldn't heal on it's own! <br /> So if the sin-eater is shot in the head, he can't recover his brain, since the body can't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read the book in ages, but I distinctly remember one of the Stricken example character descriptions had died of a brain-eating virus and the Geist &quot;provided him with a new one that works, in its way.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:22:48-08:00","id":1040310,"title":"","content":"Nyx is right. You <i>could</i> do all this stuff with chaining them up or exorcising the geist after you've downed them (according to <i>Hunter: Mortal Remains</i>, not possible without a specific ritual like the one described for Sin-Eaters), but it's much easier to just cut off the Sin-Eater's head. Or at least after you kill them, just sever their head. Removing a vital organ like the heart or brain is not necessarily enough to keep it from regrowing (see Null Mysteriis on the matter of Fog Men in <i>Mortal Remains</i>), but severing a being's head entirely is generally a good catch-all for permanent death. The real trick is to make the geist give up on repairing its host's body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T22:50:53-08:00","id":1040445,"title":"","content":"I mean, I can totally see a vengeful Geist diving down to the depths below to round up some assistance in repairing it's host and coming back being a big plot point! That could be a campaign all on its own, fighting off this angry Geist and whatever it can dig up in the underworld, all the while trying to keep the dead corpse of it's host from being recovered by it...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now I just hope my players don't read these forums, because this seems like a badass idea ^^.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12915-ktccd","name":"ktccd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T01:28:04-08:00","id":1040489,"title":"","content":"Geists can't actually <i>heal</i> their Sin-Eaters, but Plasm can do some pretty weird stuff in a pinch.<br /> <br /> Also, you'd be surprised what injuries a human body can recover from, given time. We can't regrow brain tissue, obviously, but the brain is very good at adapting and working around damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":12259,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","user":"GimpInBlack","date":". 01-30-2017, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T02:07:29-08:00","id":1040500,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer: Of course this is all my opinion and perception of how geists and their Bound work.<br /> <br /> It would probably take an extraordinary level of genuine partnership between a geist and its host to make the geist work that hard to keep them. Most have a working relationship with their Bound, but only to the extent that they can use their Bound to fulfill their own drives. In the end a Sin-Eater really is just a vessel, one that can (and will) ultimately be replaced.<br /> <br /> In any case...I'm not sure a geist could leave its host to get help in that situation, or get help at all? That seems to be part of the Bargain: As long as a geist is attached to its Bound, it can stave off the energy of death to a certain extent because it's sharing its own deathly nature with its Bound. That's not something other ephemeral entities could &quot;help&quot; with; they're not bonded to the Sin-Eater in a way that allows them to manipulate his energies. Likewise, the only geists capable of traveling on or between planes by themselves are unfettered. The whole point of joining with a Sin-Eater is to have a physical body, and the downside is that they're tied to that body until they let go of it. Once they let go, they can't stave off its death anymore; the Sin-Eater reverts to being a simple mortal and passes the threshold of death fully, unable to return except maybe as a raised zombie. If zombie Sin-Eaters were a thing, then geists wouldn't need to keep their hosts alive.<br /> <br /> I've always seen the Bargain as a kind of osmosis - the geist has a deathly nature that &quot;bleeds&quot; over to the Sin-Eater when they bond. The more the SE's physical body is damaged, the more energy the geist has to bleed over to fix it. At a certain point, fixing it either isn't feasible or just isn't a worthwhile investment anymore, and it's better to let go and look for a new mortal instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T12:30:08-07:00","id":1064422,"title":"","content":"In my hunter campaign, I have houseruled that a sin-eater has to roll psyche+synergy to resurrect, and the more closely this death replicates the original death, the harder the roll is.<br /> So killing them in the same way/in the same situation etc add penalties, while things like the exact same weapon/the same place/the same killer add large ones.<br /> <br /> The idea is that the Geist has effectively delayed that original death, and by convincing it/the underworld/death itself that the death has caught up with them, the bargain is broken.<br /> <br /> It requires some fluff changes but it does mean a hunter can actually kill a sin-eater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:03:33-07:00","id":1064442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=1064422#post1064422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my hunter campaign, I have houseruled that a sin-eater has to roll psyche+synergy to resurrect, and the more closely this death replicates the original death, the harder the roll is.<br /> So killing them in the same way/in the same situation etc add penalties, while things like the exact same weapon/the same place/the same killer add large ones.<br /> <br /> The idea is that the Geist has effectively delayed that original death, and by convincing it/the underworld/death itself that the death has caught up with them, the bargain is broken.<br /> <br /> It requires some fluff changes but it does mean a hunter can actually kill a sin-eater.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very elegant and thematic solution. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T18:39:55-07:00","id":1064598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/131497-how-do-you-kill-a-sin-eater?p=1064422#post1064422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my hunter campaign, I have houseruled that a sin-eater has to roll psyche+synergy to resurrect, and the more closely this death replicates the original death, the harder the roll is.<br /> So killing them in the same way/in the same situation etc add penalties, while things like the exact same weapon/the same place/the same killer add large ones.<br /> <br /> The idea is that the Geist has effectively delayed that original death, and by convincing it/the underworld/death itself that the death has caught up with them, the bargain is broken.<br /> <br /> It requires some fluff changes but it does mean a hunter can actually kill a sin-eater.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is indeed a very good one, I think it should be put in 2nd edition and you should receive at minimum the pulitizer prize <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2015-inspectorjavert","name":"inspectorjavert","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}